I noticed this weird problem with my linux box today. kernel 2.6.20

if my USB bluetooth dongle was already connected to the PC when it was
booting then any filetransfer done from then on hangs(freezes) without any
error messages on either my phone or the pc.

And sometimes the connection is unstable. But these same problems however
vanish once plugin the USB dongle after the system boots. Is this behaviour
unique to me or does anyone have the same problem. If it is experienced by
many ppl what might be the problem. I really need my dongle up and running
as soon as i boot without plugging it in later.



